A||||12||Homicidal||My New Headlight system + AWESOME tire pics!||||10||
Z||000000||Homicidal||08-16-2000||11:08 PM||||I got the new headlights finally!  The bulbs I am using here ARE street legal (at least in San Diego), and they cast a greenish-blue.  So you get an idea of how powerful they are, when driving on the freeway, I hit the sign WAy above me on the overpass and all the others around me, at the same time!  They cast a LONG ways!  <P>You can see the low beam cast here:<P> <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-006f.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-006f.jpg</A> <P>Here are the high beams:<P> <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-005f.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-005f.jpg</A> <P>I can remember if this is a high or low beam:<P> <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-007f.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-007f.jpg</A> <P>I also bought a pair of the Xenon Gas Charged Hyper White bulbs.  I'll throw pics of that pair up soon.  Those suckers are BRIGHT.<P>I also bought this Maguire's Tire Gel.  This stuff is GREAT!  AFter I applied it, I also sprayed my tire with a strong jet of water, didn't move that gel!  Great stuff to use, a must have for you show-car people!  These pics also show off the rims I did myself also.  Took the clearcoat off and polished the crap outta them!  <P>Tire one:<P> <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-008f.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-008f.jpg</A> <P>Tire two:<P> <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-009f.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/images/Mvc-009f.jpg</A> <P>I didn't rub it on the entire tire because<P>a) that part hits the road anyways and<BR>b) it wouldn't be safe since I would lose traction!<P>But I love this stuff!  I also decked out the black trim by using Turtle Wax: Black Chrome.  Also a quality product!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Homicidal (edited 08-16-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-16-2000||11:32 PM||||Wow! That tire gel really makes those tires look good!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Those headlights dont appear to be too bad...better than those annoying bright blue things that give me a friggin' headache!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||08-17-2000||04:29 AM||||Re-Read my post, I also have those bright ones!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||08-17-2000||07:38 AM||||I don't know if you're aware of this, but those "xenon" bulbs are somewhat brighter, but aren't the "real" bulbs that cast that blue/white light. Those lights that are so bright are actually High Intensity Discharge lights. The color is the result of high levels of ultra-violet content in the light. Those bulbs don't use a filament, and aren't direct swap-outs for standard bulbs. Those bulbs actually produce an arc inside the bulb housing, similar to an arc welder, only focused (obviously). Those systems run around 500 bucks, and require an ac invertor for operation. Aftermarket driving light kits are available, I don't know if you can even get conversion kits for "standard" bulb types like headlights.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||08-17-2000||08:39 AM||||PIAA 990s are what you'll need for a real HID install retail --- you sitting down...  $1200!!! I had a Hella Conversion kit with CATZ Iridium Lights like the ones you have and loved them... their WAY easier to drive in the rain with too!||||reg||1
