Z||000008||Homicidal||08-18-2000||03:09 AM||||Why do you say that Shiner?  The blue headlight systems are not on the ricer cars.  In fact, it was started by BMW and Mercedes.  It's a luxury, not a sports feature.  Although the ricers adopt it.<P>But I'm sick of hearing this rice-trashing when most of us are being hypocrites.<P>Defition of a ricer:  Honda model car, lowered, spoiler, nice rims and big seat belts, and bumpin' stereo.<P>What do we do?  Lower our cars, get spoiliers, etc..<P>I personally like some of the features that add to their car, like the blue headlights.<P>Now if you were referring to the tire gel, well that is just ludicrous.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Taijiguy||08-19-2000||10:02 AM||||Actually, I think the ricer thing is more about the way *many* rice-owners put appearance products on, in an effort to LOOK like they go fast. My sense is, the disrespect for them comes from being "fake". maybe the connection is, you're trying to give the impression that you have something you don't have, being "fake", as it were. Don't get me wrong, it's your car, I wouldn't for a second presume to tell you what to do, I'm merely expressing my thoughts on why that comment was made.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000010||Homicidal||08-20-2000||03:08 AM||||True, but they are wrong thoughts!  Everybody in their right mind knows a Fiero does NOT have an HID system.  Plus, everyone KNOWS the new BRIGHT halogen and xenon bulbs are avaliable, so it's not fake.  I didn't do it to try and fake it's something it's not.  I did it because bright blue or white headlights are friggin awesome!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Taijiguy||08-20-2000||10:20 AM||||True, while they may LOOK cool, for 80 bucks I would have gone with a set of Hella's or CIBIE's, and put in a set of fire-setting bright-a$$ bulbs, like 80/150's or eve 100/200's. If you think the bulbs you have are bright, you should see the ones I'm talking about! And NO, they do not blind oncoming traffic, since the pattern is very precise, and the beam cuts off at a low angle. That's what makes those lights so great, is you can run a higher wattage bulb without inflicting pain on other motorists.<BR>Just my 1/2 cent worth.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000012||Homicidal||08-20-2000||10:47 PM||||You misunderstand, my bulbs weren't $80, the headlight kits was!  <P>And mine are 130/100.||||reg||1
